WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.449 --> 00:00:12.610
Element Uuh, that’s ununhexium, 116, is
a triumph for the new

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.790
nomenclature system, the way of trying to
bring together these

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:21.270
competing labs who were trying to synthesise
these elements. Because

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:27.730
the discovery of Uuh was announced simultaneously
by a Russian lab in

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:32.250
Dubna and the Lawrence Livermore Lab in the
United States showing

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:36.090
that, at last, collaboration had come together
and scientists of all

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:40.090
countries were working together to try and
understand the chemistry of

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:46.980
these elements. What exactly the chemistry
of Uuh is, is still unclear but

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:52.400
again, using Mendeleev’s ideas we can see
that this is going to be in the

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:59.530
same group as oxygen, sulphur, tellurium,
polonium and so Uuh will be

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:04.110
rather more reactive than, or radioactive
than, polonium but will have a

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:05.540
similar sort of chemistry.

